    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0630" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v22/pg602"/>

                <head>358. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in the
                        Philippines<anchor n="1" xml:id="d358-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-08-19T18:51:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1955—6:51 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>626. Additional to penultimate sentence our 610.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d358-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>As matter of principle and in practice Department wishes avoid associating grants
                    of US aid or loans with visits by Chiefs of State to US. Such visits should
                    stand on their own merits and association of aid with state or official visits
                    creates unfortunate precedents. Loans and grant assistance must be carefully
                    considered to determine if they are useful and appropriate and in conformity US
                    policy objectives.</p>
                <p>When asking Magsaysay for firm answer re visit you may give him substance our
                    thinking this subject and explain this does not mean decision reached his
                    proposal which still under consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d358-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d358-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 411.9641/8–1955. Secret; Priority.
                    Drafted in PSA; approved in draft by Sebald and in final by Frederick E.
                    Nolting.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d358-f2" n="2" xml:id="d358-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 610, August 12, informed the Embassy of continuing efforts to obtain a
                    decision as to the availability of funds for Magsaysay’s rural development
                    program. It also expressed apprehension that Magsaysay had not yet reached a
                    final decision on his visit to the United States since considerable advance
                    planning was necessary for a State visit. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi>
                    411.9641/8–1255)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
